Make backend run status, transcript/history, tool progress, usage/statistics and command-output state observable through canonical data and frontend projections rather than state-bearing TuiSubmitResult fields, event adapters that construct TUI objects, or presentation callbacks that recompute backend state. Inspect runtime_active_run_internal.*, runtime_submit_internal.*, event_state.*, app event adapters, interactive_tui_support.cpp and SessionStats. Preserve streaming responsiveness and the existing distinction between authorized conversation events and local command output.

Do not replace an ordered event stream with a single coalescing dirty bit. Where events are required, use a backend-owned bounded sequenced journal/canonical accumulation with frontend cursors or an equivalently verified neutral delivery protocol; specify ordering, session/request identity, acknowledgments, overflow/resynchronization and cancellation. The frontend pulls through projection refresh APIs and performs its own rendering reductions. Preserve every tool result, permission-related ordering, ordinary-turn authorization, compaction boundary, transcript selection/search anchor and attachment safety constraint. A mutation notification grants no authority to accept an event.

Publish SessionStats at backend-owned lifecycle/mutation points, with active_context_tokens and system_prompt_tokens updated coherently and stale computations rejected. Eliminate refresh_session_statistics requests from UI snapshot application, render and generic completion paths. In particular /exit must not reload history and republish unchanged statistics twice merely because submission completion applies a snapshot and renders. Retain legitimate final usage and persistence before shutdown. Test streaming and queued follow-ups, local command isolation, errors/cancel/quit, stale events after replacement, compaction, coalesced notifications and final statistics. Run focused event/runtime/composer tests and active-run/streaming terminal smokes; instrument recomputation counts to prove duplicate exit publication is gone.
